# id_pocket_residues.in — identify the residues lining the binding site
#
# Run once per system, on the reference structure only. The resulting residue
# list is then hard-coded into rmsd.in so that the same atoms are measured in
# every frame and every replicate.
#
# Usage: cpptraj -i id_pocket_residues.in > id_pocket_residues.log 2>&1
# Replace SYSTEM with the system name and LIG with the ligand residue name.

parm SYSTEM_dry.prmtop

# Load frame 1 only — the pocket is defined on the reference structure
trajin SYSTEM_prod_rep1_dry.nc 1 1

# Residues with at least one atom within 5 A of the ligand.
# Output lists every matching atom; collapse it to unique residue numbers.
# The ligand itself appears in the output and must be excluded from the list.
mask :LIG<:5.0 maskout pocket_residues.dat

go
